-- IELTS 8.0 (C1–C2): new points that build on 7.0, each with a lesson and a practice set of three or more objective
-- questions, a final test per chặng and a course test. Listening follows the transcripts of reused recordings.

-- New points and their prerequisites.

-- Reading: inference across a whole text.

When the national museums abolished entrance charges, visitor numbers rose by more than half within a year, and the policy was widely celebrated as a victory for access. A closer look at the figures complicates the story. Most of the additional visits were made by people who already visited museums regularly; the proportion of visitors from low-income neighbourhoods barely moved. Free entry, it seems, removed a barrier that mattered less than its supporters had assumed. None of this means the charges should return. But it does suggest that the museums'' real task, persuading people who have never felt welcome to walk through the door, cannot be accomplished by a price change alone.', 'VALID');
