Few industries have automated as quickly as warehousing. Robots now carry shelves to workers, so that staff no longer walk several kilometres a shift. Companies present this as a straightforward improvement in working conditions, and injuries from heavy lifting have indeed fallen. Workers'' accounts are more ambivalent. Many describe a job that is physically easier but more tightly monitored: every movement is timed, and targets rise whenever the system shows that they can. The technology, in other words, has changed the nature of the pressure rather than removed it.', 'VALID');
